  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Xacuti gets its distinctive dark, complex flavour from dry-roasting and grinding whole spices fresh for the dish. The process takes a little longer than opening a jar, but the difference in the final sauce is marked. Do not rush the roasting step; the spices need to smell toasted and just starting to smoke before they come off the heat."}]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {"level": 2},
        "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "What you need"}]
      },
